<rml>
<head>
	<title>VaCuus M3 Data Binding Demo</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="m3_demo.rcss"/>
</head>

<!-- `data-model="hud"` is resolved EXACTLY ONCE, in Element::SetParent, when this body is
     parented into the context (ThirdParty/RmlUi/Source/Core/Element.cpp:2202-2219). A model
     created after that attaches to nothing, and the only diagnostic is one Log::LT_ERROR --
     which DOES appear, as `LogVaCuus: Error: [Rml] Could not locate data model 'hud' ...`
     (FVaCuusSystemInterface::LogMessage routes it), but only at load time and naming this
     element rather than the missing bind. vacuus.M3Demo therefore calls BindModel BEFORE
     LoadDocument, and the queue being FIFO from one producer is what makes that ordering hold
     across the thread boundary. -->
<body data-model="hud">
	<div id="m3-title">VaCuus M3 // DATA BINDING DEMO</div>

	<!-- 1. TEXT SUBSTITUTION. `{{Field}}` is DataViewText: it evaluates the expression and
	     calls ElementText::SetText only when the value actually CHANGED
	     (DataViewDefault.cpp:354), which is the reason an unchanging model costs zero
	     published frames and also the reason "0 published frames" alone cannot tell an idle
	     model from one that dirties everything every frame. -->
	<div id="p-scalars" data-class-alert="bAlert">
		<div class="panel-title">1 &#183; SCALARS ({{Tick}} updates published)</div>
		<div class="row"><span class="key">CallSign</span><span class="val">{{CallSign}}</span></div>
		<div class="row"><span class="key">Ammo</span><span class="val">{{Ammo}}</span></div>
		<div class="row"><span class="key">Stance</span><span class="val">{{Stance}}</span></div>
		<div class="row"><span class="key">Zone</span><span class="val">{{Zone}}</span></div>
		<div class="row"><span class="key">Objective</span><span class="val">{{Objective}}</span></div>
	</div>

	<!-- 2. A BOUND VALUE AS GEOMETRY. data-style-width writes the `width` property rather than
	     text, so this bar MOVES -- which is what makes a screenshot evidence about the pipeline
	     rather than about the font. Health is a float, and RmlUi renders a bound double through
	     "%.3f" plus TrimTrailingDotZeros (TypeConverter.inl:282-295), so the label below reads
	     three decimals at most while vacuus.DumpModel prints full precision. -->
	<div id="p-bar">
		<div class="panel-title">2 &#183; FLOAT AS GEOMETRY (data-style-width)</div>
		<div id="bar-track">
			<div id="bar-fill" data-style-width="Health + '%'"/>
		</div>
		<div class="row"><span class="key">Health</span><span class="val">{{Health}}</span></div>
	</div>

	<!-- 3. A FLATTENED NESTED STRUCT. `Target.Designation` and `Target.Distance` are two layout
	     entries with one top-level name: RmlUi's DirtyVariable takes top-level names only
	     (DataModel.cpp:325-331), so both leaves dirty `Target` and one re-evaluation serves
	     them both. ParseAddress splits the dotted path and applies no name rule to the segments
	     (DataModel.cpp:9-46), which is why `Size` would be legal here and not at the top. -->
	<div id="p-nested">
		<div class="panel-title">3 &#183; NESTED STRUCT (one top-level name, two leaves)</div>
		<div class="row"><span class="key">Target.Designation</span><span class="val">{{Target.Designation}}</span></div>
		<div class="row"><span class="key">Target.Distance</span><span class="val">{{Target.Distance}}</span></div>
	</div>

	<!-- 4. ATTRIBUTES AND ONE-WAY-NESS. data-attr writes an attribute, and it too skips the
	     write when the value is unchanged (DataViewDefault.cpp:79).

	     The button is the I3 probe: `data-event-click="Ammo = 0"` reaches
	     VariableDefinition::Set, which FVaCuusScalarDefinition REFUSES -- it returns false, logs
	     once, and both RmlUi call sites then skip their own DirtyVariable
	     (DataControllerDefault.cpp:57-59, DataExpression.cpp:1185-1197). Click it and Ammo does
	     NOT change; that is the whole of M3a's one-way contract, on screen. -->
	<div id="p-write">
		<div class="panel-title">4 &#183; WRITES ARE REFUSED (M3a is one-way)</div>
		<div id="probe" data-attr-vacuus-ammo="Ammo">ammo mirrored into an attribute</div>
		<button id="write-btn" class="m3-btn" data-event-click="Ammo = 0">try to set Ammo = 0</button>
		<div class="hint">Nothing happens, by design: see vacuus.DumpModel and the LogVaCuus warning.</div>
	</div>

	<!-- 5. THE M3b KILLFEED: `data-for` over a TArray of struct rows. The div carrying data-for
	     is a hidden TEMPLATE, not the first row -- DataViewFor::Initialize sets `display: none`
	     on it and every generated row is a clone of its tag and attributes (minus data-for)
	     inserted BEFORE it (DataViewDefault.cpp:474, :523), which is why the row styling below
	     hangs off the template's own class list. `{{Killfeed.size}}` is answered by the array
	     DEFINITION's Child(), not by the RmlUi core -- the one case a hand-rolled definition
	     breaks by omission (VaCuusDataVariable.cpp:514-519).
	     data-if writes a LOCAL `display: none` when false and REMOVES it when true
	     (DataViewDefault.cpp:224-245), so the HS pill's stylesheet display is what shows. -->
	<div id="p-kills">
		<div class="panel-title">5 &#183; KILLFEED (data-for over TArray, {{Killfeed.size}} rows)</div>
		<div class="row kill-row" data-for="kill : Killfeed">
			<span class="killer">{{kill.Killer}}</span>
			<span class="k-sep">&#187;</span>
			<span class="victim">{{kill.Victim}}</span>
			<span class="weapon">{{kill.Weapon}}</span>
			<span class="hs" data-if="kill.bHeadshot">HS</span>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
